# Coverage reports. Generated, gitignored, and full of machine-absolute paths.
coverage
coverage-*

# The authoritative architecture document: one hand-authored file whose CSS and tables Prettier
# rewrites wholesale. It is cited by section number from specs, ADRs and commit messages, so it is
# ignored rather than reformatted — otherwise `pnpm format:check` is red until someone lands 4000
# lines of whitespace churn through the one document that is meant not to move.
docs/architecture.html

# Postman collection and environments. These are round-tripped through Postman's exporter, which
# owns their formatting: reformatting them here leaves `pnpm format:check` red after every export,
# for a diff nobody reads. The README beside them is not exempt.
apps/api/postman/*.json
apps/api/postman/environments/*.json

# Generated by `depcruise-baseline` and never hand-edited (spec 004, FR-013); the tool owns its
# formatting the same way Postman owns the exports above.
.dependency-cruiser-known-violations.json

# Vendored by GitHub Spec Kit (`specify init`, commit a271f81) and rewritten wholesale by its next
# upgrade; reformatting them here leaves `pnpm format:check` red after every upgrade, the same way
# the Postman exports would. Our own files under .claude/ are not exempt.
.specify
.claude/skills/speckit-*

# Converted from docs/architecture.html (ignored above) and re-converted when it changes; the
# converter owns its formatting.
docs/architecture.md

# Sandbox template scaffolds (spec 015, research R2): project files copied verbatim into a work
# dir, not repository code. Their formatting is the template author's, and the lockfiles are
# npm's.
apps/api/templates/*/files

# The SDD orchestration workspace (briefs, reports, hand-offs). Self-gitignored, so CI never sees
# it; ignored here so a local `pnpm format:check` matches CI while it exists in the tree.
.superpowers
